=== PARITY (vs web VehicleAccessWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (VehicleAccessSource -> VehicleAccessModel):
    useVehicleDrivers, useVehicleInvitations, useVehicleMobileEnabled, useVehicles, useTranslation. The
    production app wires the source over the KMP drivers/invitations/mobile-enabled stores (coalesced);
    the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> VehicleAccessProjection.driverEntries is a 1:1 port of the web `driverEntries` memo
    (label = name ?? email ?? '—'; value = formatDateShort(fetched_at); badge = role=='owner' ?
    Owner/success : Driver/neutral). invitationEntries ports the `invitationEntries` memo (label =
    created_by ?? '—'; value = formatDateShort(created_at); status pending→Pending/warning,
    accepted→Accepted/success, else→Expired/danger — web 'error' variant = danger badge). MobileAccess
    ports `mobileData?.data?.enabled ?? null` as a closed tri-state. EXECUTED + asserted (see gate [5]).
  Composition -> shell chrome (person.2 icon + "Vehicle Access" title + freshness chip + refresh + Open) ·
    1x2 CompactView (people glyph + "{n} Drivers" + tri-state mobile dot) · 2x4 StandardView (uppercase
    "Mobile Access" + Enabled/Disabled/Unknown chip, then "Authorized Drivers" detail card, then
    "Pending Invitations" detail card shown only when invitations exist — web invitationEntries.length>0).
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSTone / TSSkeleton +
    ContentUnavailableView (compiled against the real macOS 15 SDK in gate [2]). VehicleAccessChip mirrors
    the TSBadge tokens, extended to take a pre-localized String (our per-surface table) the
    LocalizedStringKey-only TSBadge can't express. VehicleAccessDetailCard/Row port the web WidgetDetailCard.
    Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No access data available") · error (retry
    affordance) · stale (freshness chip + "Reconnecting — access may be stale" banner) · offline (cached
    values + chip + "Offline — showing last known access" banner) · content (compact OR standard). Model
    phase resolution keeps cached content visible behind refresh/errors, matching the web shell. EXECUTED
    truth-table assertions in gate [6].
  i18n -> all source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
